ref{section-big-small}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{groupoids-example-constant-group}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-representable-sheaf-fpqc}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-constant-locally-constant-maps}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:438315d6cf315706f69e5464d5f39093b5b10cce40010692ccc5ab99bcdcd4d9", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:4139357aba98b0d1a889c37b3643399f22eb6c7cfe1f78f699c94ca4abac52b9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:11ee3e77ac4aa07a4e2534769e968259089dd68e8f8bb5362c177422f6d23b6c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an abstract group.\nOn any of the sites <MATH_0002> or <MATH_0003> of\nSection <REF_0001>\nthe sheafification <MATH_0004>\nof the constant presheaf associated to <MATH_0005> in the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>Zariski topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of the site already gives\n<MATHSEG_0001>Zariski locally constant maps <MATHSEG_0002>\nThis Zariski sheaf is representable by the group scheme <MATH_0006> according to\nGroupoids, Example <REF_0002>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0003>\nany representable presheaf satisfies the sheaf condition for the\n<MATH_0007>-topology as well, and hence we conclude that the Zariski\nsheafification <MATH_0008> above is also the <MATH_0009>-sheafification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d5e342967e1bfe3422d1248f471bde65b6f0b4efde40eafb8ad4819f51234c4", "unit_id": "tag:03P5:statement"}
